  "dom_id": "question-148085",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "A gambling room has three roulette tables, table $1,$ table $2,$ and table $3.$ Data of all bets of a particular evening are collected.\n\n- $30%$ of bets were played at table $1,$ and $5%$ of those bets were won.\n\n- $35%$ of bets were played at table $2,$ and $6%$ of those bets were won.\n\n- $35%$ of bets were played at table $3,$ and $7%$ of those bets were won.\n\nIf $10%$ of bets were played in the first hour, and $4%$ of bets made in the first hour were won, what is the probability that a randomly chosen winning bet was played in the first hour? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
